			"Description": "Mahler Symphony No1 with Music Director Thomas S\u00F8nderg\u00E5rd. \n\n0:30 Movement I: Langsam, Schleppend (Slow, dragging) - Immer sehr gem\u00E4chlich (Always at a very leisurely pace)\n15:45 Movement II: Kr\u00E4ftig bewegt, doch nicht zu schnell (with strong movement, but not too fast) - Trio: Recht gem\u00E4chlich (Quite leisurely) - Tempo primo\n23:25 Movement III: Feierlich und gemessen, ohne zu schleppen (Solemn and measured, without dragging)\n34:28 Movement IV: St\u00FCrmisch bewegt (Stormy)\n\nIf you enjoyed this performance and would like to support the RSNO, please consider donating at https://www.rsno.org.uk/support-us/playyourpart/.\nText RSNO 5 to 70085 to donate \u00A35\nText RSNO 10 to 70085 to donate \u00A310\nText RSNO 20 to 70085 to donate \u00A320\n\nThis performance was recorded on Saturday 5 October 2019 at the Glasgow Royal Concert Hall. The concert was dedicated to the RSNO Conductors Circle. Original audio feed courtesy of BBC Radio 3.",
